      "meta_description": "A small side street opposite my hotel. I found most of the shops closed most of the time on this street, as they had not opened with I was leaving in the morning, and they had closed by the time I reached in the evening, after my sightseeing. I ate several times in an Islamic Restaurant (Restoran Islamic) on this street (the white sign you see just above the white van's roof) which dished out delicious and flaky egg paratha (bread) and kopi tarek (literally 'pulled coffee'- more on that later). (Sandakan, Sabah, East Malaysia, Nov.2013)       "
